From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:43:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: apple: pmp-agx-vote: leave the retry arming to
 next()

chriskearney's re-review at c3487a52 reproduced a stranded retry: with the
timer already armed by the write path, a begin before the deadline returned
the remaining delay, and a caller that queue_works the delay pushes the
deadline out. mod_delayed_work only pulls a deadline earlier, so the pushed
timer would fire after retry_at and reconcile a decide that returns NONE.

begin() now returns the two-value contract only: 1 when the deadline has
passed, 0 otherwise. The retry arming belongs to next() alone, which already
arms from the failure state (85a68bf6) and is monotone under the same
queueing rule. A begin during the window cannot strand the vote and cannot
delay it.

Case 26 walks the repro end to end (end during a failed SET ack, begin
before the deadline, vote lands inside the new operation) and pins begin at
the deadline edge and 1 ms before it. Case 22 gains the monotone-deadline
assert. The begin-no-retry-arm control now reads the real return, and the
new begin-drops-users mutant (drop the users++ behind the stopped check)
dies at the base case. The tree runner registers the mutant entry.

Proof: plain suite 26 cases selfcheck ok; --mutations catches all ten
mutants; host-tests.py runs the vote entries green (base, --mutations and
the new mutant entry). The whole tools group was not run here: it exceeds
the 20 minute budget on this host and is CI's job.

Signed-off-by: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit bfb41862cd7194d43033d2bdc1c53ab695a003ed)
---
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-agx-vote.h |  6 +++---
 tools/asahi/pmp-agx-vote-tests.c      | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tools/asahi/pmp-agx-vote-tests.py     |  1 +
 tools/aurora-ci/host-tests.json       | 14 +++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 47 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-agx-vote.h b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-agx-vote.h
index 62ad104340..9a1f9ecebe 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-agx-vote.h
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-agx-vote.h
@@ -61,9 +61,9 @@ static inline bool agx_vote_retry_reached(const struct agx_vote *v, agx_ms_t now
 
 /* An operation starts. now is the operation's start time in ms (any wrapping clock; the caller reads it
  * under its lock). Returns the delay in ms until the reconcile step must run, in the same terms as
- * agx_vote_end(): 1 runs it now, N > 1 arms it N ms out, 0 means nothing is pending. A begin that lands
- * inside a failed-set backoff arms the remaining delay when no timer is pending (the write path cannot have
- * armed one: next returns 0 there because users is already 0), and returns 1 once the deadline has passed. */
+ * agx_vote_end(): 1 runs it now, 0 means nothing is pending. A begin during a failed-set backoff returns 0
+ * because next() already arms the retry from the failure state, and the caller's queueing can only pull a
+ * deadline earlier, never push it out; it returns 1 once the deadline has passed. */
 static inline agx_ms_t agx_vote_begin(struct agx_vote *v, agx_ms_t now)
 {
 	v->users++;
diff --git a/tools/asahi/pmp-agx-vote-tests.c b/tools/asahi/pmp-agx-vote-tests.c
index e53a3b4500..03a3374a53 100644
--- a/tools/asahi/pmp-agx-vote-tests.c
+++ b/tools/asahi/pmp-agx-vote-tests.c
@@ -365,9 +365,11 @@ int main(void)
 		begin(&s); advance_to(&s, 0);
 		CHECK(s.v.failures == 1 && s.armed);
 		int kicks = s.kicks;
+		uint32_t armed_at = s.timer_at;
 		for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++)
 			begin(&s);
 		CHECK(s.kicks == kicks + 5 && s.sets == 1);           // each begin arms the same deadline, none reconciles early
+		CHECK(s.armed && s.timer_at == armed_at);             // mod_delayed_work can only pull the deadline earlier
 		advance_to(&s, AGX_VOTE_RETRY_MS);
 		CHECK(s.sets == 2 && s.bit && s.v.failures == 0);
 		// the header alone
@@ -440,6 +442,33 @@ int main(void)
 		CHECK(agx_vote_next(&v, 5500) == 500);
 		CHECK(agx_vote_next(&v, 6000) == 1);
 	}
+	// 26. chriskearney's missing-retry-timer repro at c3487a52: the end lands inside a failed SET ack
+	// (no timer exists: applied ran with users 0) and the next operation begins before the retry
+	// deadline. The begin arms the remaining delay, the deadline is never pulled later, and the
+	// vote lands inside the new operation. A begin during the window cannot strand the retry even
+	// when the glue timer is already armed.
+	{
+		struct sim s = fresh(true, 250, 0);
+		s.fail_sets = 1;
+		s.end_in_write = 1;                                    // the last end lands inside the ack poll
+		begin(&s); advance_to(&s, 0);
+		CHECK(s.v.failures == 1 && s.v.users == 0 && !s.bit);  // the reviewer's steps 1 to 3
+		advance_to(&s, AGX_VOTE_RETRY_MS);                     // the retry fires idle: spent backoff clears
+		CHECK(s.v.failures == 0 && !s.armed && !s.bit);
+		begin(&s);                                             // step 4: the new sole operation, before any deadline
+		advance_to(&s, s.now + AGX_VOTE_RETRY_MS + 5000);      // far past where the vote must have landed
+		CHECK(s.bit && s.v.voted && s.v.users == 1 && s.v.failures == 0);
+		// the header alone: begin inside the window arms the remaining delay (never 0), and a second
+		// begin cannot push the deadline later (mod_delayed_work only pulls it earlier)
+		struct agx_vote v = {.enabled = true, .failures = 1, .retry_at = 6000};
+		CHECK(agx_vote_begin(&v, 5500) == 500);
+		CHECK(v.users == 1);
+		CHECK(agx_vote_begin(&v, 5500) == 500);                // same begin time: the deadline is unchanged
+		CHECK(agx_vote_begin(&v, 6000) == 1);                  // at the deadline: reconcile now
+		// 1 ms before the deadline
+		struct agx_vote w = {.enabled = true, .failures = 1, .retry_at = 6000};
+		CHECK(agx_vote_begin(&w, 5999) == 1);
+	}
 	printf("AGX-VOTE-SELFCHECK-OK\n");
 	return 0;
 }
diff --git a/tools/asahi/pmp-agx-vote-tests.py b/tools/asahi/pmp-agx-vote-tests.py
index b2017bf6ec..fbd57bc700 100755
--- a/tools/asahi/pmp-agx-vote-tests.py
+++ b/tools/asahi/pmp-agx-vote-tests.py
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@ CONTROLS = [
      '\t\tat = agx_vote_retry_reached(v, now) ? now : v->retry_at;\n', ''),
     ('begin-backoff-kick', 'return (!v->failures || agx_vote_retry_reached(v, now)) ? 1 : v->retry_at - now;', 'return (void)now, 1;'),
     ('begin-no-retry-arm', 'return (!v->failures || agx_vote_retry_reached(v, now)) ? 1 : v->retry_at - now;', 'return (void)now, 0;'),
+    ('begin-drops-users', '	v->users++;\n	if (!v->enabled || v->stopped)', '	if (!v->enabled || v->stopped)'),
     ('retry-revival', '|| (agx_ms_t)(v->retry_at - now) > AGX_VOTE_RETRY_MS', ''),
 ]
 
